{"type":"text","timestamp":1794589550862,"sessionID":"ses_e2a256410ffejPK5IfFGf0oN97","part":{"id":"prt_1d5df521b002VGe2bzDMvuGhVY","sessionID":"ses_e2a256410ffejPK5IfFGf0oN97","messageID":"msg_1d5df160f001jVMuVsibyQofZi","type":"text","text":"T016 is complete. The new test was written first and failed for exactly the predicted reason, then the source change made it pass.\n\n**Files written**\n\n1. `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts` — added `it('refuses a row id in the session form')` inside `describe('reader failure')` at line 628. It runs `--runtime claude --locator '{\"sessionId\":\"session-1\"}' --row-id no-such-row` and expects status 2, empty stdout and stderr containing `--row-id narrows --summary only`.\n2. `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs` — `selectMode` now throws `new UsageError('--row-id narrows --summary only')` when `options.rowId !== null`, placed after the `--runtime` and `--locator` checks (line 123). The ` [--row-id <id>]` fragment was removed from the `--runtime` usage line in both the header comment and `USAGE`.\n\n**Verify output**\n\nFirst run, before the source change, failed as the task predicted:\n\n```\nAssertionError: expected '{\"ok\":false,\"code\":\"locator_unavailab…' to be '' // Object.is equality\n+ {\"ok\":false,\"code\":\"locator_unavailable\"}\n Test Files  1 failed (1)\n      Tests  1 failed | 60 passed (61)\n```\n\nAfter the change:\n\n```\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\n      Tests  61 passed (61)\n```\n\n`rg -c -e '--locator .*\\[--row-id' <S>` printed nothing and exited 1, so no match. Extra sanity check: `node --check` on the scorer exited 0.\n\nBaseline before the new case was 60 passed, so all 60 existing cases still pass and the 61st is the new one. The scoped diff is two files, 17 insertions and 3 deletions. The tasks.md checkbox is not ticked.\n\n**Status and handback**\n\nThe work is uncommitted and dirty on branch `worktrees/352-command-surfacing-research`. Nothing was committed, pushed or reverted, and no file outside the two named ones was edited.\n\nObserved: the new session-form refusal and the six-case `--summary` suite are green. Inferred, not exercised: `--summary` with `--row-id` still narrows, because the summary branch returns before the new check. No test passes that flag pair, so only the code read supports it. Known residual risk: none beyond that blind spot.\n\nThe `README.md` row for the scorer still says `--row-id` narrows either mode. That sentence is T018's file and task, so it is expected to change next, not a missed edit. Nothing is blocked on the operator.","time":{"start":1794589544987,"end":1794589550862}}}
